Refurbished Linux 0.3.0-r3 — hardware round: Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, audio, media keys

file:   refurbished-linux-0.3.0-r3-amd64.iso
size:   824180736 bytes
sha256: 7262e2dc5470fc4ee41e67ac22f58d9a6c1e73ff203edd061e7d950f3d9417e1
firmware: BIOS (isolinux) + UEFI (grub efi.img), isohybrid MBR+GPT
base:   Debian 13 trixie, kernel 6.12.117-amd64

Fixes, with evidence, in docs/hardware-0.4.md:
  - wpa_supplicant was missing entirely -> Wi-Fi could never scan or join
  - bluetooth.service was never enabled -> no adapter, no scanning
  - PipeWire/WirePlumber were never started -> no sound, bar said "Muted"
  - volume slider had a hidden mute hit area -> volume appeared to reset
  - setuid bits were missing -> sudo/su unusable in every earlier image
  - source dirs 0700 were copied into the image -> login "no shell"
  - Microsoft 365/Outlook/OneDrive/Teams launchers removed

Verified in QEMU/OVMF: desktop boots; Bluetooth, NetworkManager and
wpa_supplicant active; Wi-Fi scan returns a test AP; 2s of sine captured
from the emulated codec (peak 23844); media keys move the volume; 160%
amplification works; mute does not return.
Unverified: real radios, real codecs, brightness hardware, OSD overlay.
